{% extends "models/base.twig" %}
{% block pageName %}Privacy Policy{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
<div class="page narrow prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">What's stored, and why.</p>

    <h2>If you have an account</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Your username, profile blurb, and the date you signed up. These are public on your profile.</li>
        <li>Your email, only if you gave one. It isn't shown to anyone.</li>
        <li>Your password, stored as a one-way hash. Nobody can read it, including us.</li>
        <li>The IP address you signed up from and last signed in from, stored encrypted. It's used to stop people from making piles of alt accounts.</li>
        <li>The games you've favorited. These are public on your profile.</li>
        <li>Your friends list, and how many friends you have (the number is public on your profile).</li>
        <li>Messages and images you send friends. Only you and the person you're talking to can see them, unless one is reported: then moderators see it and the messages around it.</li>
        <li>When you were last on the site, so friends can see if you're online.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>One cookie keeps you signed in. Your browser also remembers whether you collapsed the sidebar. There's no ad tracking.</p>

    <h2>Other services</h2>
    <p>Some parts of the site load things from other companies, who can see your IP address when they do:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Cloudflare, for the captcha on sign-up</li>
        <li>YouTube, for the video on the sign-in and sign-up pages</li>
        <li>Google Fonts, cdnjs, unpkg and jsDelivr, for fonts, icons and emoji</li>
        <li>Each game, which may load its own scripts or ads</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Deleting your account</h2>
    <p>Ask and your account and everything attached to it will be deleted.</p>
</div>
{% endblock %}
